mi workspace per client. Connect the client&#x27;s mailboxes and social accounts. Run separate sequences in separate workspaces without paying per seat per client.</p><div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 bg-[#FAFAFA] border border-[#e4e4e7] text-[12px] text-[#52525b]"><span class="text-[#a1a1aa]">Example:</span><span class="italic">“<!-- -->For ClientCo: sequence dental practice owners in Texas with 4-plus stars on Google<!-- -->”</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="w-full bg-[#fafafa] py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-24"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is sequencing really free on every paid plan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The Sequencer is included on Starter, Pro, Scale, Ultra, and Enterprise at no extra cost. There is no per-seat fee, no per-send fee, and no add-on subscription. You only pay for the underlying paid plan you already have."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does unlimited actually mean? Are there deliverability caps?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Unlimited means Origami does not put an artificial cap on how many messages you can schedule or send from a connected mailbox or social account. Real-world deliverability limits set by Gmail, Outlook, and the social platforms still apply, and we recommend warming a new mailbox before high-volume sending. Multi-account rotation is included to keep volume per account inside healthy ranges."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I connect multiple social accounts and email inboxes?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Connect as many mailboxes and social accounts as you want. Origami rotates sends across the connected accounts, respects daily limits per account, and shows replies from every account in one shared inbox."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does it handle time zones?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Each step in a sequence has its own send window. Origami sends inside that window in the lead's local time zone when one is available, and falls back to the workspace default otherwise. You can also pause sending on weekends and on holidays."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where do replies show up?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every reply lands in a single inbox inside Origami, regardless of which channel or which connected account received it. Replies automatically pause the sequence for that lead so you do not send a follow-up to someone who already responded."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does this integrate with the agent?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sequencing lives in the same surface where you research. Build a list in a table, then ask the agent to enroll those rows into a sequence with a specific template. The agent moves the leads into the sequence without an export step."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What sequence steps are supported?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Up to 10 steps per channel, with email and social messages as native step types. You can mix channels in a single sequence, add wait conditions, and branch based on whether the lead replied or opened."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a free trial?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. You can try Origami end-to-end on the Free Trial. The Sequencer is unlocked the moment you start any paid plan, with no separate purchase."}}]}</script><div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6"><h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium tracking-[-0.3px] text-center mb-8 sm:mb-10 text-[#09090b]">Frequently asked questions.</h2><div class="border-t border-[#e4e4e7]"><div class="border-b border-[#e4e4e7]"><button aria-expanded="false" class="flex w-full items-center justify-between py-5 text-left cursor-pointer group"><span class="text-[15px] font-medium text-[#1c1917] pr-4">Is sequencing really free on every paid plan?</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.